DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The iinnssmmnnttqquuee() function associates a vnode with a mount.  This includes
     updating _v___m_o_u_n_t for the vnode, and inserting the vnode into the mount's
     vnode list.

     The indirect mount reference count, maintained as the count of the vnodes
     owned by it, is incremented for each vnode added to the mount, and that
     reference is decremented by vgone(9).

     The mount's interlock is held while the vnode is inserted.  The vnode
     must be exclusively locked.

     On failure, iinnssmmnnttqquuee() resets vnode' operation vector to the vector of
     deadfs(9), clears _v___d_a_t_a, and then calls vgone(9) and vput(9).  If more
     elaborated cleanup after iinnssmmnnttqquuee() failure is needed, the iinnssmmnnttqquuee11()
     function may be used instead.  It does not do any cleanup following a
     failure, leaving all the work to the caller.  In particular, the opera‐
     tion vector _v___o_p and _v___d_a_t_a fields of the vnode are kept intact.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The iinnssmmnnttqquuee() function will always return 0, unless the file system is
     currently being unmounted in which case it may return EBUSY.  Also,
     iinnssmmnnttqquuee() may be forced to insert the vnode into the mount's vnode list
     by setting the _V_V___F_O_R_C_E_I_N_S_M_Q flag in the vnode _v___f_l_a_g, even if the file
     system is being unmounted.

